# 1️⃣ Longest Common Subsequence (LCS)

## Problem

Find longest sequence present in:

```text
Both Strings
```

Order must remain same.

---

### Example

```text
s1 = abcde

s2 = ace
```

Answer:

```text
ace
```

Length:

```text
3
```

---

# 2️⃣ State Definition

```cpp
dp[i][j]
```

Meaning:

```text
LCS length
between

s1[0...i]

and

s2[0...j]
```

---

# 3️⃣ Recurrence

If characters match:

```cpp
1 +
dp[i-1][j-1]
```

---

Otherwise:

```cpp
max(
dp[i-1][j],
dp[i][j-1]
)
```

---

### Formula

```cpp
if(s1[i]==s2[j])

dp[i][j]
=
1+dp[i-1][j-1];

else

dp[i][j]
=
max(
dp[i-1][j],
dp[i][j-1]
);
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N*M)

Space: O(N*M)
```

---

# 4️⃣ LCS Tabulation

```cpp
for(int i=1;i<=n;i++)
{
    for(int j=1;j<=m;j++)
    {
        if(
            s1[i-1]
            ==
            s2[j-1]
        )
        {
            dp[i][j]
            =
            1 +
            dp[i-1][j-1];
        }
        else
        {
            dp[i][j]
            =
            max(
                dp[i-1][j],
                dp[i][j-1]
            );
        }
    }
}
```

---

# 5️⃣ Print LCS

After building DP table:

Start from:

```text
dp[n][m]
```

Move backwards.

---

### If Match

```text
Take Character
```

Move diagonally.

---

### Else

Move towards larger value.

---

### Complexity

```text
O(N+M)
```

